                <pb facs="0780" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg648"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163/65: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-10-13T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 13,
                                1926—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 13—9:35
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>476. My 453, October 5, 10 a.m. British Legation have received a telegram from
                    British missionary near Sianfu, dated October 12th, indicating that all British
                    and American missionaries who desired to leave are safely out of Sianfu.
                    American military officer will not therefore proceed to Sianfu unless report
                    proves incorrect.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
